# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
Promise.all([(await promise as Foo).bar]);
Promise.all([(await promise)!]);
Promise.all([await promise as Foo]);
Promise.all([await promise satisfies Foo]);
Promise.all([<Foo>await promise]);
Promise.all([await promise!]);
Promise.all([(await promise)<Foo>()]);
Promise.all<Foo>([await promise]);

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:15 lint/nursery/noAwaitInPromiseMethods ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This await delays the call to Promise.all().
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ Promise.all([(await promise as Foo).bar]);
      │               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ Promise.all([(await promise)!]);
    4 │ Promise.all([await promise as Foo]);
  
  i The rest of the array and the call to Promise.all() have to wait until this promise finishes, so the promises don't run at the same time.
  
  i Move the await into an async function that you call right away, or use .then() instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

